commit 2cb59ad4309ae9b1dce4bdfc7503b42cfa8d588d
Author: Alazer Manakelew <alazermanakelewb@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 9 19:29:46 2026 -0400

    support for dia (#262)
    
    * feat(dia): scaffold DiaConfig (encoder/decoder/model/data)
    
    * fix(descript-dac): drop output_padding in decoder transpose convs
    
    The decoder's WNConvTranspose1d layers passed outputPadding: 1, adding one
    sample per stage (4 stages) and shifting the decoded waveform. The reference
    Descript DAC uses no output padding (kernel 2*stride, padding ceil(stride/2)),
    which makes each stage an exact integer upsample. Removing it yields output of
    exactly frames * hop_length and matches the reference to ~1e-4.
    
    * feat(dia): port Nari Labs Dia-1.6B to Swift
    
    Encoder-decoder transformer TTS: byte-level text encoder, GQA self-attention
    plus MHA cross-attention decoder over 9 delayed DAC codebooks with
    classifier-free guidance, decoded to 44.1 kHz by the Descript audio codec.
    
    - DiaConfig/DiaLayers/DiaAudio/DiaTTSModel with T5-style DenseGeneral,
      half-split RoPE, concat KV cache, precomputed cross-attention KV.
    - Registered in the TTS factory (case "dia") with repo-name inference.
    - Encoder, first decode-step logits, and full greedy waveform match the
      Python mlx-audio reference to a relative error of ~1e-4 (float32).
    - Config-decode, model-build, and model-type resolution unit tests.
    
    * Fix tests and update for API changes.
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: Lucas Newman <lucas@future.fit>
    Co-authored-by: Lucas Newman <lucas@future.fit>
    Co-authored-by: Lucas Newman <lucasnewman@me.com>

